=[nonum]{contributors} About the Authors
These are the authors who contributed to this book.@<br>{}
The affiliation, title, and profile of each author are as of the time of writing.

==== Minhyuk Kim
CyberAgent, Inc. SGE Core Technology Division / Client Engineer

Responsible for planning and coordinating this book, and for writing the Prologue and the introduction to Part 3, "@<title>{editorial-intro-3}", among others. @<br>{}
After serving as a lead engineer and engineering manager at several smartphone game development companies, he joined the SGE Core Technology Division (Core Tech) as a mid-career hire in 2023. He is responsible for quality assurance of in-house projects and has worked on performance tuning of released titles. From his position in a cross-organizational team, he now works on building mechanisms that raise application quality across the company, going beyond individual cases.

//noindent
Unite Tokyo 2019 "Optimization Techniques You Should Learn Now for Production"@<br>{}
CEDEC2024 "Assure the Quality of Mobile Games! Recommending Performance Monitoring"@<br>{}
Unite Seoul 2025 "Efficient In-House Unity Project Quality Management Strategy and Optimization Cases"

==== Takayuki Kiyohara / X: @nezumimusume
CyberAgent, Inc. SGE Core Technology Division

Responsible for writing the introduction to Part 1, "@<title>{editorial-intro-1}", and "@<title>{kiyohara-takayuki-1}".

After working for 13 years at a game developer in Osaka, mainly on domestic and overseas game development for game consoles, he moved to a vocational school for training game creators and spent about six years training the next generation. During his time as an instructor, he wrote "HLSL Shader Grimoire".
He currently works as a Unity graphics engineer at the SGE Core Technology Division (Core Tech) of CyberAgent's Game & Entertainment Division.

//noindent
CEDEC+KYUSHU 2022 "Training Graphics Engineers with an In-House Game Engine"@<br>{}
CEDEC+KYUSHU 2023 "In the Age of Game Engines, We Dared to Teach How to Build a Software Renderer in New-Graduate Training"@<br>{}
CEDEC2024 "Introducing the Development of an Integrated Stylized Rendering System: Aiming for a Foundation That Can Be Shared"@<br>{}
CEDEC2025 "Visual Regression Testing with Unity Graphics Test Framework"@<br>{}
CEDEC2026 "Trying Anime 4K on Mobile"

